# Index Big5 of the WHATWG Encoding Standard, Big5 with the Hong Kong
# Supplementary Character Set, both ways: the tables `chinese.hero` reads.
#
# The table is data, made and not typed: a one-off Heroes program,
# `gen_tables.hero`, which is not in the tree (defect 2639), read the WHATWG
# Encoding Standard's resources, fetched from encoding.spec.whatwg.org on
# 2026-11-17, as the standard says to read them, packed them, held every
# packed value to the value it read, and wrote this module whole. Nothing here
# is edited by hand. What it read:
#
# - `index-big5.txt`, Identifier 8dfc771062e7be0810919082c2c06baa2236147909e0ecc235b1cb9ad782ac82, Date 2024-09-18

# The code point of each pointer of index Big5, from 0: pointer `p`'s is bits
# `21 * (p % 3)` up of word `p / 3`, 21 bits, 0 where the index has none.
constant DECODE: [i64]
